And-- but next year, it was even worse. And they didn't even call me anymore. In fact, I was then the only Jewish pupil among 600 children-- 300 in the gymnasium and 300 in the high school. All the other Jewish boys-- it was all-- it was a boys' school at the time, not a mixed school-- all the other boys had left, and either emigrated, or went to other schools.

