INT: Where was your mother at this stage?

HH: My mother at this stage lived together with an aunt in Fulda.

INT: Where was that?

HH: Fulda is in-- in-- in middle Germany, I should say. It was a very Orthodox community. And my father was actually born there. So an-- an aunt of mine, who was unmarried, lived there in the house of the grandparents. And my mother moved in with her in 1941. And she was then deported in May 1942 to the East. Well, we never heard anything from her anymore.

INT: Was that entire town--

HH: Not the entire town. My aunt was still left behind. She was deported in early September 1942 to Theresienstadt. And a few days later, she was transported from Theresienstadt to Auschwitz. And her fate is, of course-- she had-- didn't have a chance. She was a elderly person. I'll come to that later on. The elderly people didn't have a chance. [PAUSES FOR 4 SECONDS]

