HH: That's right. And in the evening, I had a temperature of 41 degrees from all the excitement. You can imagine how I felt. But of course, I quietened down very soon again, and everybody congratulated me that I got out of that transport. Because, of that particular transport, not a single person survived. They all were subsequently-- those that arrived alive in Auschwitz went into the gas chambers.

