All I can say to-- to those who may see this video and may listen to this interview is you can possibly forgive. I mean, the young German generation is very embarrassed, themselves, of what their parents and grandparents did to us. That I have experienced many times myself. They are very embarrassed themselves. They can't understand how this ever happened. But you cannot forget.

INT: So generally now your feeling towards the Germans living today is not that they bear any culpability for what happened?

HH: Not the young generation-- the young generation [PAUSES FOR 3 SECONDS] cannot understand themselves what their parents and grandparents did to us.

INT: In retrospect, do you have strong feelings towards the rest of the Gentile world, who some people say sat back and did nothing while the Jews were being gassed? And--

